# f_ion demand scan on the W2 rho2M vertical point — DIAGNOSIS.
#
# WHAT QUESTION THIS ANSWERS. HANDOFF_S3_ION_2026-08-09.md establishes that the
# ion term IS the sim's 10-90 % rise-time floor (`--no-ions` lands on the data
# at every quantile) and that the electronics axis is exonerated (the beta scan
# moves undershoot linearly and moves the rise by 4 ns). What nobody has
# measured is the SLOPE: how much rise-time does a unit of f_ion buy? Without
# it "f_ion must be wrong" is unfalsifiable, because it does not say BY HOW
# MUCH, and the T14 session cannot fit beta jointly against a term whose
# derivative is unknown.
#
# This scan measures dRise/df_ion directly, at fixed everything else.
#
# THE DIAL. `--ion-model analytic` splits the induced charge f_e prompt /
# f_ion over a rectangle of length g^2/(mu V) = 306.1 ns, and kernel_lut's
# apply_ion_transit mixes them linearly (`f_electron * blk + f_ion * run`).
# f_ion = 1 - z_aval/gap and the rectangle's LENGTH does not depend on z_aval,
# so --z-aval-um moves f_ion and NOTHING else. That is the only clean f_ion
# dial the chain has; the measured template welds the split to the calib.
#   z_aval 105 um -> f_ion 0.30
#   z_aval  75 um -> f_ion 0.50
#   z_aval  45 um -> f_ion 0.70
# These are DIAGNOSIS probes of a charge split the detector does not have.
# None of them is a physics proposal — 13.84 um / f_ion 0.9077 is the measured
# value and the scan exists to say how far from it the data sits.
#
# THE CURVE THIS COMPLETES (X view, 10-90 % rise p5, ns):
#   f_ion 0      DIAGNOSIS_noions        142   (exists)
#   f_ion 0.30   this scan                 ?
#   f_ion 0.50   this scan                 ?
#   f_ion 0.70   this scan                 ?
#   f_ion 0.9077 DIAGNOSIS_ionanalytic     ?   (cluster 3919446)
#   f_ion 0.9006 DIAGNOSIS_noisefix      254   (exists, measured template)
#   DATA                                  150
#
# PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION (written before any of these ran, 2026-08-09):
#   p5 rises monotonically and CONVEXLY with f_ion, because the 10-90 % rise
#   is set by whichever component dominates the leading edge and the prompt
#   spike keeps control until the ion share is large. Concretely: f_ion 0.30
#   lands at 150-175 ns, 0.50 at 175-205, 0.70 at 205-235. The data's 150 ns
#   is then met at f_ion ~= 0.25-0.35 — i.e. the data demands a split THREE
#   TIMES smaller than the measured 0.90, not a 10-20 % correction.
# FALSIFIER: if the curve is instead concave or near-flat below f_ion ~ 0.8
#   (f_ion 0.70 already at or under 165 ns), then rise is insensitive to f_ion
#   over most of its range, a modest f_ion error CAN explain the floor, and the
#   claim above is wrong.
# SECOND FALSIFIER: if p5 at f_ion 0.30 is still well above 150 ns, then NO
#   value of f_ion reproduces the data at this transit time, the defect is not
#   the split at all, and the next axis is the transit/template speed or the
#   longitudinal x lateral factorisation itself.
#
# Single-variable against DIAGNOSIS_ionanalytic: same kernel, calib, noise,
# clusters, beta = 0.75 default, ion-model analytic. Only --z-aval-um moves.
universe                = vanilla
executable              = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/run_stageBC_w2.sh
MY.SendCredential       = true
request_cpus            = 4
request_memory          = 16000
+MaxRuntime             = 7200
log                     = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/w2.log

NOISE = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/calib/noise_det3_satscan_feu07.json

arguments               = "rho2M DIAGNOSIS_fion030 $(NOISE) '' '--ion-model analytic --z-aval-um 105.0'"
output                  = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_fion030.out
error                   = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_fion030.err
queue

arguments               = "rho2M DIAGNOSIS_fion050 $(NOISE) '' '--ion-model analytic --z-aval-um 75.0'"
output                  = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_fion050.out
error                   = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_fion050.err
queue

arguments               = "rho2M DIAGNOSIS_fion070 $(NOISE) '' '--ion-model analytic --z-aval-um 45.0'"
output                  = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_fion070.out
error                   = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_fion070.err
queue
